worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_native_lanes.js"
  ceiling 444
  rationale "Browser twins of native precedence rows the worker used to leave to the Rust engine (PR #1188, issue #1175 routing probes): agentic_continuation (the seeded handler-rules.lino rule), meta_explanation (rust/src/solver_handlers/meta_explanation.rs: why / how-you-work / architecture questions read from seed roles), how_it_works (the inline-subject mechanism discovery plan of rust/src/solver_handler_how.rs, offline as native renders it), source_refresh and shell_command_transform (rust/src/retrieval_procedures.rs, rust/src/solver_handlers/shell_command_transform.rs; cue words are `source_refresh` / `shell_command_transform` records of data/seed/code-task-cues.lino) and the response-language demonstration (rust/src/meta_method_answers.rs). Every answer renders a seeded response template from data/seed/multilingual-responses-synthesis.lino or multilingual-responses.lino; growth is the ported handlers, not silent regrowth. Raised to 396 for two recogniser boundaries mirrored from Rust: shellTransformCommandSpan (a plain-word prose lead ending at a colon is not part of the looped command, mirroring command_span) and whyQuestionAddressesAssistant (a fronted why-question claims meta_explanation only when it carries an assistant_self_reference word, mirroring addresses_assistant). Raised to 461 for the bare how_it_works branches of try_how_it_works: a bare mechanism_inquiry phrase (isBareHowItWorks, mirroring is_bare_how_it_works) reads its topic from the previous assistant reply (howItWorksPriorTopic, mirroring extract_topic_from_prior_reply with the seeded topic_scan_stop_word role), answers a known topic through the concept lookup, an unrecorded one with the seeded how_it_works_prior_topic response, and no prior reply with the seeded how_it_works_no_context response. Ceiling moved to 462 for issue #1175 R3 (follow-up round, 2026-10-08): the source refresh records source_refresh:refusal when it names no source. Lowered to 444 for issue #918 (2026-10-08): the source-refresh twin is the source_refresh seed rules run through runHandlerRuleSet; its cue records and stable-id helper are gone."
